(5426525, 777487, 84363, '<td valign="top">Really nice photo.  I personally like the Dave Matthews version of this song better!</td>', 'Really nice photo.  I personally like the Dave Matthews version of this song better!', '2009-04-08 11:48:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5427084, 777104, 66635, '<td valign="top">I realize I''m biased, but I think this is a freaking hilarious photo - especially when combined with the title!  I also think it''s well-composed.  I couldn''t do anything about the other people in the shot and realize they constitute a distraction for some.  Also, the shot is very noisy because of the low light.  I used ISO 6,400 and no flash - I don''t like flashes.  Other than the noise and the other people in the background, this is one of my favorite shots.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-08 13:39:16.</i></td>', 'I realize I''m biased, but I think this is a freaking hilarious photo - especially when combined with the title!  I also think it''s well-composed.  I couldn''t do anything about the other people in the shot and realize they constitute a distraction for some.  Also, the shot is very noisy because of the low light.  I used ISO 6,400 and no flash - I don''t like flashes.  Other than the noise and the other people in the background, this is one of my favorite shots.', '2009-04-08 14:38:23.000000', '2009-04-08 14:39:16.000000', 0),
(5427144, 777104, 56502, '<td valign="top">I don''t find it noisy, actually. Gave it a 7. But being from Munich I''m biased too. Did you visit Bavaria, or is this somewhere else?<br/> <br/>And the feather - the Gamsbart (although admittedly it looks more like a feather) is the pride of the dancer. Can''t be distracting by definition.<br/> <br/>Btw, you beat me by one place - my entry is the next one.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-08 14:17:50.</i></td>', 'I don''t find it noisy, actually. Gave it a 7. But being from Munich I''m biased too. Did you visit Bavaria, or is this somewhere else? And the feather - the Gamsbart (although admittedly it looks more like a feather) is the pride of the dancer. Can''t be distracting by definition. Btw, you beat me by one place - my entry is the next one.', '2009-04-08 15:14:26.000000', '2009-04-08 15:17:50.000000', 0),
(5427162, 777458, 56275, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club! <br/> <br/>Well I agree with the voters and commenters. This is a breathtaking shot. You did a great job bringing back detail with the tone mapping. I love that the photo keeps my attention. My eyes wander across the bottom, along the bridge, and through the sky line, exploring the scene. <br/> <br/>I agree with MemberTygerr that breaking the skyline with the hill in the background would have made it stronger. Currently, the sky almost looks like a gradient border. If you''re skimming past the photo, I don''t think you''d realize just how amazing that sky is. If you were to re-shoot, I wonder if you could get lower, and maybe even bring the radio tower on the right, above the sky line? It''s a great scene. I''d be shooting it all the time if I were there. =)<br/> <br/>Obviously you met the challenge well. I can''t really think of anything else to improve this photo. Except perhaps taking it earlier in the evening to capture even more of the detail. But then again, the night shot really gives it a great mood. Nicely done.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-08 14:41:07.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Well I agree with the voters and commenters. This is a breathtaking shot. You did a great job bringing back detail with the tone mapping. I love that the photo keeps my attention. My eyes wander across the bottom, along the bridge, and through the sky line, exploring the scene.  I agree with MemberTygerr that breaking the skyline with the hill in the background would have made it stronger. Currently, the sky almost looks like a gradient border. If you''re skimming past the photo, I don''t think you''d realize just how amazing that sky is. If you were to re-shoot, I wonder if you could get lower, and maybe even bring the radio tower on the right, above the sky line? It''s a great scene. I''d be shooting it all the time if I were there. =) Obviously you met the challenge well. I can''t really think of anything else to improve this photo. Except perhaps taking it earlier in the evening to capture even more of the detail. But then again, the night shot really gives it a great mood. Nicely done.', '2009-04-08 15:40:37.000000', '2009-04-08 15:41:07.000000', 0),
(5427177, 776733, 56275, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First off, good job meeting the challenge. No disputes there. It''s a cute picture, however, that said, the photos isn''t very intriguing. It doesn''t do a great job at keeping the viewer''s attention. It''s a good photo, but not particularly great. <br/> <br/>Angle: I like the POV you chose for this shot. Getting down on the ground can be a great way to get a unique capture. <br/> <br/>Composition: I like the crop you chose. Gives the user a defined focal point. Behind the boot on the left, there''s something flesh-toned in the background. Not sure what it is.. but it''s a bit distracting. <br/> <br/>Subject: The boots themselves are pretty flat and uninteresting. I wonder if work boots would have been better.. Probably not on DPC. DPC voters tend to like bright colors. Perhaps adding a kid in the boots, covered in mud? Or stomping in a muddy puddle?<br/> <br/>Lighting: Seems a bit hazy and dark. It was probably a cloudy day.. but would have bumped the exposure or levels in post processing. Bumping the saturation would help too.<br/> <br/>Good idea, just needs a few tweaks to make it great.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First off, good job meeting the challenge. No disputes there. It''s a cute picture, however, that said, the photos isn''t very intriguing. It doesn''t do a great job at keeping the viewer''s attention. It''s a good photo, but not particularly great.  Angle: I like the POV you chose for this shot. Getting down on the ground can be a great way to get a unique capture.  Composition: I like the crop you chose. Gives the user a defined focal point. Behind the boot on the left, there''s something flesh-toned in the background. Not sure what it is.. but it''s a bit distracting.  Subject: The boots themselves are pretty flat and uninteresting. I wonder if work boots would have been better.. Probably not on DPC. DPC voters tend to like bright colors. Perhaps adding a kid in the boots, covered in mud? Or stomping in a muddy puddle? Lighting: Seems a bit hazy and dark. It was probably a cloudy day.. but would have bumped the exposure or levels in post processing. Bumping the saturation would help too. Good idea, just needs a few tweaks to make it great.', '2009-04-08 15:56:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5427348, 777475, 102259, '<td valign="top">Wow! A portrait hasn''t leapt of the page and screamed "LOOK AT ME" in my ear in a long long time. This is brilliant. Certainly my favourite of the bunch! I love everything about it!</td>', 'Wow! A portrait hasn''t leapt of the page and screamed "LOOK AT ME" in my ear in a long long time. This is brilliant. Certainly my favourite of the bunch! I love everything about it!', '2009-04-08 17:39:40.000000', NULL, 0),
